  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "If $f''(x)=18\\cos 3x$ and $f'(0)=f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=1$, find $f(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(x)=-2\\cos 3x+x+1-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f''(x)&=18\\cos 3x\\\\f'(x)&=6\\sin 3x+C_1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $f'(0)=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}0+C_1&=1\\\\C_1&=1\\\\f'(x)&=6\\sin 3x+1\\\\f(x)&=-2\\cos 3x+x+C_2\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-2\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\pi}{2}+C_2&=1\\\\-2(0)+\\frac{\\pi}{2}+C_2&=1\\\\C_2&=1-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\f(x)&=-2\\cos 3x+x+\\left(1-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
